# aptberg soft_exclude list: fnmatch globs against Package names.
#
# You can reference this file from aptberg.yaml through the
# "soft_exclude" filter.
#
# Drops names an include glob (e.g. "*") matched. Dependencies still
# win: a soft excluded package that something needs is mirrored anyway.
# Names listed literally in include are kept even when matched here.
#
# Sizes: jammy + noble (+ -updates, -security), main restricted universe,
# amd64, measured 2026-09-22. include ["*"]: 1389G; with this list: 396G.

# Versioned kernel packages: every ABI ever published in -updates, times
# every flavour (generic, aws, gcp, azure, oracle, lowlatency, nvidia,
# ...), plus prebuilt nvidia modules per kernel and driver
# (linux-objects-nvidia-*, ~700G alone). The unversioned metapackages
# (linux-generic, linux-image-aws, linux-generic-hwe-22.04, ...) are not
# matched and pull in the ABI they currently point at, so each snapshot
# carries the current kernel of every flavour. Saves ~975G.
linux-*[0-9].[0-9]*.[0-9]*-[0-9]*

# Kernel source tarballs, several hundred MB per ABI. Saves ~9G.
linux-source-*

# dotnet source-build artifacts, only used to build dotnet itself.
# Saves ~9G.
*-source-built-artifacts

# Candidates if more is needed (not enabled):
#   *-doc     saves ~20G
#   *-dbg     saves ~12G
#   texlive-* saves ~3G
